comments.body:
@reporter , sorry for inconvenience. The issue [2262](https://github.com/onnx/tensorflow-onnx/issues/2262) you mentioned is going to be fixed by [this PR](https://github.com/onnx/tensorflow-onnx/pull/2279). With a new release of TF2ONNX later, you can use the latest version of ONNX to work.

Currently, I see you've already converted your TF model to an existing ONNX file. So please upgrade your ONNX to latest version 1.15.0, and then call your code "converted_model = version_converter.convert_version(onnx_model , 19)", it should convert the opset version to 19.

I tried this workaround for one ONNX file and it works. Please feel free to let me know if it doesn't work for you.

@participant2 thank you for your effort!

I updated my packages now to ONNX 1.15.0 and tf2onnx 1.16.0. However, if I try to use opset version 19/20 I still run into this exception: `ValueError: make_sure failure: Opset 19/20 is not supported yet. Please use a lower opset` and if I use a lower opset I run into the exception that I originally reported in this issue.

So, it seems that the issue https://github.com/onnx/tensorflow-onnx/issues/2262 was solved, but the problem with the function `onnx.version_converter.convert_version()` still exists.
